From 492ae5f8af319d2c89f88aeea4f41a6dc8f00e68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: laughtt <22533943+laughtt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:20:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] pimax: controller-driven hand tracking
 (XR_EXT_hand_tracking, data source CONTROLLER)

The Dream Air controllers now also expose XRT_INPUT_HT_CONFORMING_LEFT/RIGHT with get_hand_tracking:
u_hand_sim_simulate_generic() on joint curls computed by the Rust crate pimax-hands (trigger -> index, grip ->
middle/ring/little, touch bits -> thumb via filters and a thumb state machine). The C side only feeds it the decoded
reports and poses the hand at grip pose * grip->wrist offset (also from pimax-hands). Linked through libpimax_capi.a
(pimax-capi re-exports the pimax_hands_* C ABI, so there is one Rust staticlib); with the C libpimax the driver links
libpimax_hands.a instead.

Switches: PIMAX_CTRL_HANDS=0 turns it off. PIMAX_CTRL_HANDS_DEMO=1 replaces the reports by a scripted pattern (test
aid; controllers then also exist with PIMAX_NO_DEVICE=1, without attach thread or reports).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
